  "title": "# Build: settings-placement-everywhere (FABLE: settings-placement@1 is a shared contract) ## What B…",
  "asked": "# Build: settings-placement-everywhere (FABLE: settings-placement@1 is a shared contract) ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"Set the settings interface for Molly to open in a dialog.\" ... \"I should be able to select in every screen where its settings pops up.\" Book to a free named agent. ## Do 1. **Land PR #289 (plugin-settings-placement) first.** It's RED with conflicts: update from main, resolve, CI green, merge. Give its `settings-placement@1` contract the Fable review its report asked for and fix anything found. 2. **Every screen, every app** (console, Molly, AmberX web, axHub web, Expenses) gets a per-screen setting for where its settings open: **dialog / side panel (left or right) / bottom sheet / inside the screen / full page / floating window**. Also an app-wide default plus 'use app default' per screen. 3. Reachable from: right-click / long-press on the screen's settings button or title ('Settings opens in...'), the app's Settings > Settings placement list showing every screen, and console controls so Amber can set it by voice (add a control target, e.g. `settings.placement`, to axf-console's control surface). 4. **Set Molly's settings to open in a dialog** as soon as it works. 5. Fix what #289's report flagged: panels close instantly with no animation, and only the Terminal hosts settings 'inside'. Add the wrapper so any screen can. 6. Settings render through the `settings-interface@1` asset, coordinating with tab-group-assets (default + per-app custom, shared default selected). 7. Rule in RULES.md / PORTING.md, tests, UI Review shots (non-blocking), PR, auto-land, redeploy. Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. ## ADDENDUM 1 (Brett, voice, Nov 4) \"Every settings interface should have a setting to declare where it pops up.\" - Placement is a **field on the `settings-interface@1` asset itself** (`opensIn`: dialog / side panel L|R / bottom sheet / inside / full page / floating window, plus size and animation), shown as a 'Pops up in' row at the top of every settings interface. - Precedence: the per-screen override, then the settings interface's own `opensIn`, then the app default. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
